From 6125946f9c8d474e5b601b58dd69c8453d974eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:46:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): clear a stale adoptedRunningTurn when this
 window starts a turn

adoptedRunningTurn marks a turn this window resumed onto mid-run: it never
received the prompt row, so the settle path must hydrate stored history.
Only the normal message.complete branch consumes the flag. When the adopted
turn ends any other way (Stop -> cancelRun plus the interrupted late
complete, an error frame, a running=false heartbeat settle), the flag stays
true and leaks into the next turn this window submits itself. With a
non-empty final, the stale flag alone makes shouldHydrate true, forcing a
redundant stored-transcript fetch and reconcile over a reply that is
already on screen.

Clear the flag where this window originates a turn: the submit optimistic
seed and the restore/edit/regenerate optimistic arms. It is deliberately
not cleared at message.start: a subagent watch window resumes with
running=true and then receives a synthetic message.start from
tui_gateway's child mirror for that same adopted turn, which still needs
its hydrate. Settle paths are left alone too, since a heartbeat can
precede an adopted turn's reordered message.complete (#119569). A
backend-originated next turn (queue drain elsewhere, goal follow-up) can
still inherit a leaked flag; that only hydrates a turn whose prompt this
window did not author.

Tests: a fresh submit and the rewind/reload arms clear a leaked flag; an
adopted watch turn that receives message.start still hydrates on settle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
